<section class="section wrap faq-list deep-faq"><h2>Deep cleaning questions</h2><details><summary>What&#8217;s the difference between a regular and a deep clean?</summary><p>A regular clean keeps a maintained home tidy: kitchen and bathroom surfaces, dusting and floors. A deep clean adds the detail work, like degreasing the stovetop and hood, descaling taps and glass, and hand-wiping baseboards, frames and switches.</p></details><details><summary>How often should I book a deep clean?</summary><p>Most homes book one for a first visit, a seasonal reset or before guests. After that, regular visits keep your home maintained between deep cleans.</p></details><details><summary>Is cleaning inside the oven and fridge included?</summary><p>No. Inside the oven, inside the fridge, grout scrubbing, inside cabinets and interior windows are add-ons. Ask when you book and they&#8217;ll be listed in your quote.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to provide cleaning supplies?</summary><p>No. Your cleaner brings their own supplies and equipment. Prefer your own products? Just tell us and we&#8217;ll use them.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to be home?</summary><p>No. Share your entry arrangements and we&#8217;ll arrange access with you before your visit. Keep door and alarm codes out of your booking request.</p></details><details><summary>What if I need to cancel?</summary><p>Cancel or reschedule free with at least 24 hours&#8217; notice. Cancellations with less than 12 hours&#8217; notice are charged 50% of the visit, and cancellations once your cleaner arrives are charged in full.</p></details><details><summary>Are your cleaners background-checked and insured?</summary><p>Yes. Every Elite Clean Pro cleaner is background-checked and insured.</p></details></section>
